<title>HONG KONG: HK securities watchdog probes trading in 11 stocks.</title>
<headline>HK securities watchdog probes trading in 11 stocks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong said on Tuesday trading in shares of 11 companies remained suspended due to enquiries by the Securities and Futures Commission into &quot;unusual trading movement&quot;.</p>
<p>The statement gave no further information on the suspensions or enquiries.</p>
<p>The companies are:</p>
<p>Chun Wo Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Chevalier Development International Ltd</p>
<p>Singapore (HK) Properties Investment Ltd</p>
<p>Shenzhen International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>AWT World Transport Holdings Ltd  </p>
<p>Yiu Wing International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Continental Mariner Investment Co Ltd</p>
<p>Hansom Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Lippo Ltd</p>
<p>Hongkong China Ltd</p>
<p>HKCB Bank Holding Co Ltd</p>
<p>Trading was suspended in the counters between the end of April and early June.  </p>
<p>The exchange gave no indication of when trading would resume.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6369.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
